WEBVTT

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.500
Wow!

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.120
Thanks for the meal.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.460
And for saving me.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:05.460
Who are you?

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:08.380
We're <i>shirabyoshi</i>. I'm Shizuka.

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:09.170
Tsuki.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:10.260
Akari!

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:12.880
Biwa.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.550
Do you play the biwa?

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:16.600
--Play it.
--Play for us!

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:17.810
Please!

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:55.170
THE HEIKE STORY

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:14.170
Episode 9

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.630
I'm so sweaty!

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:14.010
It's cold!

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:18.050
Come join us, Biwa!

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:26.810
Biwa.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:31.770
Hey, if you have nowhere to go,
why not come with us?

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:32.900
Where?

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.070
I dunno. All over.

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:39.200
Wherever there are people
to watch our dances.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:46.580
I just got back after a long journey.
Things seem dangerous in the capital.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:52.040
Everyone's saying it's worse with Kiso no
Yoshinaka than it was with the Heike.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:56.670
What a strange color.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:04:00.300
But I've seen someone else
with the same eye color.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.970
Where?!

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.100
In Tango province.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.560
I met her last time I was there.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:08.600
She supposedly used to
be a <i>shirabyoshi</i>, too.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:21.780
Kiso no Yoshinaka's soldiers
ransack people's homes

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:24.200
and set upon any woman they see.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:24.200
No!

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:27.040
Everyone risked their lives in battle.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:30.830
That deserves a suitable reward!
Right, Kanehira?

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.460
Yeah. Sure does.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:40.800
How dare he shield himself
with the title I gave!

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.680
I need to have him defeat
the Heike quickly,

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:47.850
but the Heike have the Emperor and the
Sacred Treasures in their possession!

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:56.780
Even if it is temporary,

00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:00.240
such a plain place is not fit
to be an imperial residence.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.700
Please make do for now, Mother.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.410
Dazaifu is an office for
administration of Kyushu.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:10.790
I hear Emperor Go-Shirakawa has had
a new emperor accede to the throne.

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:14.960
I hear he is a child of the late Emperor
Takakura and Lady Shokuko

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.710
and is called Emperor Go-Toba.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:20.420
For there to be two emperors...

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.970
No.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:23.760
There is but one emperor.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.220
Brother! Lord O--

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:35.150
Lord Ogata has received
a decree to pursue the Heike.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.310
What?!

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:40.740
You don't mean... he'll attack Dazaifu?

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:49.040
Lord Ogata once served Shigemori.
Let's send Sukemori as a messenger.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:55.420
Koremori has not been reliable since
his defeat by Yoshinaka at Kurihara.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:01.260
Lord Sukemori, what a
fine man you've become.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:07.600
Lord Ogata, I am informed that you
are gathering troops to attack my clan.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:10.890
As I have been so ordered by
Emperor Go-Shirakawa...

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:13.810
You served my father, did you not?

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:18.440
Believe me, I have no desire
to point weapons at the Heike.

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:20.320
Thus, please!

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:22.740
I beg that you leave Dazaifu!

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:28.620
He said to leave Dazaifu?

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:32.370
He said that... he could not
oppose the palace.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:42.880
I can't believe this. First we flee
the capital, then Fukuhara...

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:46.010
And now we must flee Dazaifu too?

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:49.430
If we don't, he'll probably attack.

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:50.180
But that's... I--

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:52.020
We won't run with our
tail between our legs.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:54.230
We must fight!

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:03.030
Kiyotsune, what're you spacing
out over here for?

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:06.280
You have to get ready for battle.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:11.700
I can't believe that even someone who
once served Father would attack the clan.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:15.790
That's just how the world works!

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:18.630
You have to join the
stronger side or suffer.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:23.340
But then, what about loyalty,
and uprightness, and obligation?

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:28.260
Do they really... mean nothing?

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:35.730
You think the Heike had those things?

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:41.980
Enough.

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.360
Just get ready.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:55.910
They didn't put up a
proper fight and just fled?

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:58.330
They did attack Lord Ogata's estate,

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:00.920
but they must have realized
they stood no chance.

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:05.760
The Heike are said to be heading
to the harbor at Hakozaki on foot.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:17.060
Lady Tokuko, are you all right?

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:18.100
Thank you.

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:26.190
I am fine. Please, prioritize
yourselves right now.

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:28.030
Lady Tokuko...

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:30.320
We will make it to Hakozaki alive!

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:35.580
Mother, you are soaking wet.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:39.540
Where are we going in this terrible rain?

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:42.330
Somewhere you can live in peace, Emperor.

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:48.470
Let's go. Things will be better soon.

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:02.980
Lord Kiyotsune.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:06.190
Pick yourself up. I shall walk with you.

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:09.610
Walk?

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:10.150
Yes!

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:12.820
How long must we walk?

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:16.030
How far?

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:19.750
Everyone is siding with
the Genji and betraying us.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.710
We are fish,

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:24.580
fish caught in a net.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.500
Lord Kiyotsune...

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.340
Have heart.

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:30.170
We swore together

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:33.180
that <i>we </i>would fight,

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:35.890
fight bravely and heroically!

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.390
Lord Kiyotsune.

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:43.440
Why don't we find some
shelter from the rain?

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:44.940
I'll play my flute for y--

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:46.480
I'm sorry.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:57.280
The sea really is nice.
We don't have this at the capital.

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:58.740
But it's the capital.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.250
It's not the middle of nowhere like this.

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:02.250
True.

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:06.790
What's wrong? You don't like the sea?

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:13.550
I hear that the Heike is adrift at sea.

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:15.430
That seems to be the case.

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:18.220
After all the influence
they boasted at the capital.

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:38.030
After all that walking, we finally
reached Hakozaki's harbor.

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:41.330
Yet every time we try to land,
the enemy appears.

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:44.790
We have to spend another
night on these boats.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.710
Fish caught in a net...

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:51.630
It's something Lord Kiyotsune said.

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:56.430
Are you sure you don't
want to be on his boat?

00:10:56.430 --> 00:11:00.510
Lord Kiyotsune just seems
so different now...

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:09.810
This flute playing... it's Lord Kiyotsune!

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:11.730
Biwa?

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:22.410
Lord Kiyotsune is playing his flute!
I'll join in!

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:43.640
Kiyotsune!

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:07.410
Lord Kiyotsune! Lord Kiyotsune!

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:08.370
Kiyotsune!

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:11.000
Lord Kiyotsune! Quick! We must save him!

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:13.130
Biwa!

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.090
Not again.

00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:16.840
It happened again.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:19.760
First Shigemori, and then Kiyomori...

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:21.180
And I,

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:24.060
I can do nothing!

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:26.060
Oh, Kiyotsune!

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:27.390
I see it.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:29.060
I can only see it.

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:31.270
I can't change it!

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:41.450
Were you crying all night?

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.450
Of course. You finally get
to see her, after all.

00:12:57.550 --> 00:13:00.340
Hey, it's not nice to laugh!

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:25.240
Ma!

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.920
You are just as I saw.

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:37.920
All this time, I saw you.

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:41.470
Oh, Asagi.

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:43.550
"Asagi?"

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:45.890
That's your name.

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:48.010
Pa never called me that.

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:53.600
Because it's the color of
your eye, which he feared.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:58.690
And now <i>I </i>am called by that name.

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:01.440
As the monk did...

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:02.900
I longed to see you in person.

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:09.200
If you saw me this whole time,
why didn't you come see me in person?

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:16.080
I abandoned you and your father,

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:19.750
and went to live with...
an Echigo Heike...

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:23.510
Then,

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:27.550
I shouldn't have come.

00:14:32.020 --> 00:14:33.390
Forgive me!

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:40.480
No, you don't have to forgive me.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:46.660
Thank you... for coming to see...
a mother like me, Asagi.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:55.420
It's Biwa.

00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:00.750
My name is Biwa.

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:04.800
Biwa...

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:08.510
I couldn't do anything for you...

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:10.930
...but I was always praying for you.

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.480
Praying?

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:15.390
And for your Pa, too.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:17.270
"Please, may he rest in peace."

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:19.520
"Please, may he rest quietly."

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:20.610
"Please..."

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:23.490
"Please..."

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:28.070
"May he rest in peace.
May he rest quietly..."

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.990
Even if you can't do anything...

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:32.700
Pray.

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:38.460
You're leaving now?

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:42.210
I've decided to witness the Heike's fate.

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:47.180
I'll witness it, and put my
prayers into my biwa playing.

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:49.390
I found something I can do.

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:52.970
Thanks, Ma.

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:02.400
I'll be praying, too.

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:06.440
That you get to live quietly here.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:11.280
Please, please,

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:12.870
be well.

00:16:19.170 --> 00:16:22.420
Word is that the Heike,
who had been wandering at sea,

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:25.800
defeated Lord Kiso no Yoshinaka's
army at Mizushima.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:26.720
They won?

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:30.720
In the battle at Mizushima,
the Heike's commander Tomomori...

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:38.520
...ordered his men to place
planks between their boats,

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:42.980
and is said to have fought
as if he ruled the ocean.

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:44.940
And what of Lord Yoshinaka?

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:49.200
Emperor Go-Shirakawa ordered
him to attack the Heike, but...

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:52.280
I want you to make me Shogun.

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:53.780
Is he crazy?

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:56.120
Emperor Go-Shirakawa was infuriated,

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:59.620
and employed warrior monks
to attack Yoshinaka, but...

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:02.500
<i>I </i>ran the Heike out of the capital!

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:07.300
Lord Yoshinaka burned the palace and
confined both him and Emperor Go-Toba.

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:10.130
Emperor Go-Shirakawa
seeks your assistance.

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:11.010
Goodness...

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:14.640
What's more, it is said that
Yoshinaka intends to attack <i>you</i>,

00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:18.560
and make himself head of the Genji.

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:20.980
So then... should I attack Yoshinaka?

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:22.940
Of course!

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:25.150
Hmm. Who should--

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:30.200
Make your younger brother
Noriyori the commander, and...

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:33.030
Why not send Lord Yoshitsune?

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:37.330
You're really going west?

00:17:37.330 --> 00:17:38.540
Yeah.

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:40.290
Although Yoshinaka has...

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:43.500
Dammit. Dammit!

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:45.210
Kanehira!

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:50.170
...been killed by the Kamakura Genji,

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:55.140
the same Kamakura Genji are supposed to
be headed west to attack the Heike next!

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:58.350
I have to go.

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:02.690
Thanks for everything.

00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:06.150
Take care. I'll be in
the capital for a while.

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:10.190
Hopefully the Kamakura Genji
aren't ruffians.

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:19.660
Who is the Heike's commander?

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:24.670
One known as Taira no Sukemori,
but he has already fled.

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:30.630
The remaining soldiers are
holed up at Ichinotani.

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:34.050
It's time to show your mettle!

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:38.220
Shoot! Shoot!

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:51.280
The Heike are fighting in three groups
under Tomomori, Yukimori, and Tadanori.

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:53.400
We'll launch a surprise attack from here.

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:57.660
Lord Yoshitsune?! The wild deer
may pass through here, but...

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:00.870
If a deer can do it, then so can a horse.

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:02.200
Quite right!

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:05.750
You'll be all right.

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:07.080
If we hold here--

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:09.040
Brother!

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.670
The back has already fallen!

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:11.800
What?!

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:16.720
Yoshitsune's army descended from
Hiyodorigoe and attacked from behind.

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:19.300
Then the soldiers will come here, too!

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:22.850
We'll head to the beach
and board our boats.

00:19:22.850 --> 00:19:23.810
Run!

00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:25.890
Hurry! The boats will leave!

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:32.900
We swore together

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:35.820
that <i>we </i>would fight--

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.490
fight bravely and heroically!

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:41.450
To show our backs to the enemy...

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:43.950
Lord Atsumori?

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:45.290
Go on ahead!

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:21.370
You there! I take you to be
a commander of renown!

00:20:21.370 --> 00:20:24.660
You would show your back to the enemy?

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:46.930
♪ He beckons with his fan raised. ♪

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:53.110
♪ Thus beckoned, Atsumori turns back. ♪

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:15.920
Atsumori...

00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:42.490
♪ Ready to take his foe's head,
he pushes the helmet away to see, ♪

00:21:42.490 --> 00:21:49.370
♪ A boy of 16 or 17,
features possessed of beauty. ♪

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:55.920
♪ He takes pity, and is struck by
a desire to spare his foe ♪

00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:58.340
♪ when ♪

00:21:58.340 --> 00:22:00.720
♪ he sees coming up behind him... ♪

00:22:01.680 --> 00:22:03.430
Just take my head already!

00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:10.230
Taking my head should
bring you renown, too.

00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:15.560
I swore...

00:22:16.610 --> 00:22:18.280
I swore...

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:22.650
...that I...

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:26.070
...admirably...

00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:27.660
...as a warrior...

00:22:47.640 --> 00:22:49.430
I swear.

00:22:50.640 --> 00:22:52.980
I'll pass down your story.
